# Savefiles that are known not to load, and why.
#
# One "name: reason" a line; '#' comments. The suite treats a listed file's
# refusal as expected, and also fails if a listed file *loads* -- a manifest
# that outlives its reason would silently excuse the next real break.
#
# Take an entry out when the file loads again, rather than leaving it here.
#
# This file held all thirty-five between 2 and 3 September 2026. It holds four
# now, and the difference is the point: an object whose kind has been renamed
# or removed is no longer fatal. The character wakes up without it -- see
# rd_item() and boggyman_took_one() in load.c -- and the other thirty-one
# characters came back.
#
# These four are refused for a different reason, and deliberately. DEC-50
# replaced the Life realm's spells, and a character's known spells are recorded
# by flat position across their class's books. There is no honest way to read
# them: the file says "spell 7" and spell 7 is now a different prayer. A
# missing object is visible the moment you check your pack; a Priest quietly
# holding somebody else's spell list is not. So this refuses rather than
# guesses, and that is the rule -- content can be dropped, identity cannot be
# invented.
Ador: caster; spells recorded by position against the pre-DEC-50 spell list
Amanwe: caster; spells recorded by position against the pre-DEC-50 spell list
Hilia: caster; spells recorded by position against the pre-DEC-50 spell list
Nath: caster; spells recorded by position against the pre-DEC-50 spell list
